            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery to the left atrial fistula after resection of atrial appendages.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e26-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a fistula formation between the left circumflex coronary artery draining into the left atrium as a complication of radiofrequency cardio-ablation and resection of the atrial appendages. This complication was diagnosed with the use of transesophageal echocardiography and was subsequently confirmed on coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
